{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK agent has a tool that lists files from the user's Google Drive and right now it's using a service account JSON key someone committed to the repo months ago (yes I know). Need to switch it so the tool calls Drive as whoever is actually logged into the chat, via OAuth. Also the refresh token is ending up in session.state and I can see it in the event history in the dev UI, which is... not great. How should I restructure this? Deploying to Cloud Run, demo for the client is Friday."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Building a support agent with Google ADK that needs to create tickets in our customers' Zendesk and HubSpot accounts. Each end user connects their own account. Questions: where do I store the per-user tokens and our app's client secret (currently env vars in the Agent Engine deployment), how do I handle when a user revokes access or the token expires mid-conversation, and how do I guarantee user A's tool call never picks up user B's token when sessions run concurrently? Would appreciate a concrete pattern, not just 'use Secret Manager'."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "our agent on Cloud Run keeps getting 403 PERMISSION_DENIED when it calls Vertex AI Gemini. the runtime service account is the default compute one. what role am I missing?? been staring at IAM for an hour", "needs_instead": "Basic GCP IAM troubleshooting: granting the Cloud Run runtime service account the right Vertex AI role (e.g. roles/aiplatform.user) and checking the API is enabled. This is the agent's own infrastructure access, not acting on behalf of signed-in users or managing their credentials."}
]}
